<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  MAC APP STORE ENTITLEMENTS — the smallest set that lets this app do its job.

  Every entitlement is a permission Apple's reviewer will ask you to justify, so this asks for
  two and no more:

    app-sandbox     Mandatory for the store. Nothing ships without it.
    network.client  The app talks to xearn.com/api for chat, sign-in and chain reads. Outbound
                    only — it never listens, so network.server is deliberately absent.

  DELIBERATELY NOT REQUESTED, and worth knowing why:
    files.user-selected  — the app reads and writes nothing on disk but its own container.
    network.server       — it accepts no connections.
    print, camera, mic, location, address-book, calendars — untouched by this app.

  A sandboxed app cannot spawn executables, which is why open_external calls NSWorkspace
  instead of running /usr/bin/open. That one line was the whole barrier.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
